{
 "id": "roots-society",
 "part": "Δ",
 "el": "Ρίζες της ζωής και της κοινωνίας",
 "title": "Root families: life, birth, people, city, home, law, rule, power",
 "level": "B1–C1",
 "intro": [
  {
   "p": "The roots of public life. Read a Greek newspaper and you meet these on every line: **δημ-** (δήμος, δημόσιος), **πολιτ-** (πολίτης, πολιτική), **νομ-** (νόμος), **αρχ-** (αρχή, αρχηγός) and **κρατ-** (κράτος, δημοκρατία)."
  },
  {
   "tip": "Each family starts from a root, often in two or three shapes (the present stem, the aorist stem, the ε/ο switch). The Greek verb under the heading is the everyday word that still carries the root; where the everyday word is different (παίρνω for λαμβάνω, γυρίζω for στρέφω) both are given."
  }
 ],
